  "techniqueFacts": [
    "grilling is traditional (ga nuong = grilled chicken); a very hot pan gives the same char and caramelisation (3 sources)",
    "longer marinade is the flavour lever: 15 min works, 1 hr to overnight is best, past 24 hr texture degrades (all 4 sources)",
    "rinse cooked vermicelli in cold water to stop sticking; serve at room temperature (3 sources)",
    "nuoc cham rests ~20 min so flavours meld; taste-adjust sweet/sour/heat (2 sources)",
    "tamari swap for the soy sauce makes the dish gluten free; rest of the dish (rice noodles, fish sauce) is naturally GF (1 source explicit)",
    "boneless thigh preferred for juiciness; breast is an accepted substitute (2 sources)",
    "whole-stalk lemongrass marinade: pick pieces off chicken before slicing (1 source)",
    "two sources use premade nuoc cham (0.5 cup) instead of making the sauce from scratch",
    "spoon leftover marinade over chicken while pan-cooking to build glaze (1 source)",
    "dress-and-toss or dip-as-you-go both observed; keep sauce separate for packed lunches (1 source)"
  ],
